Review round for the 0.2.1 patch release. Five independent agents read
764fb2b, one for each declared review. Each received its criteria, the
diff and the repository path, and nothing from the driver's thread. All
five verdicts are PASS.

An earlier round against this branch returned four blocking findings,
every one a defect in the patch rather than in the repository, and all
four are fixed here. The workspace loop did not route member
directories through the new check. An error split chose between two
messages by testing for one project layout when the repository supports
two, so an ordinary workspace member was told it had no project. Two
tests asserted a substring the superseded text also carried, so
restoring that text left the suite green. One guard was unreachable
through the default listing kind.

Minor findings stay in the evidence lines below and go to follow-up
issues after the merge. Two are prose this branch introduced: a
dangling "From that point" in the README, and "loop" where the
repository says "cycle". One is worth its own issue: every error routed
through `into_diagnostic` drops its declared help text, so several
pre-existing refusals ship without the remedy they declare.

